          ],
          "return_type": "Self",
          "is_static": true,
          "is_generic": false,
          "docs": "Construct a `Timestamp` from the number of 100 nanosecond ticks since 00:00:00.00,\n15 October 1582 (the date of Gregorian reform to the Christian calendar) and a 14-bit\ncounter, as used in versions 1 and 6 UUIDs.\n\n# Overflow\n\nIf conversion from RFC 9562 ticks to the internal timestamp format would overflow\nit will wrap."
        },
        {
          "name": "from_unix_time",
