              "type_name": "u8"
            }
          ],
          "return_type": "Self",
          "is_static": true,
          "is_generic": false,
          "docs": "Construct a `Timestamp` from a Unix timestamp and up to a 128-bit counter, as used in version 7 UUIDs."
        }
      ],
      "docs": "A timestamp that can be encoded into a UUID.\n\nThis type abstracts the specific encoding, so versions 1, 6, and 7\nUUIDs can both be supported through the same type, even\nthough they have a different representation of a timestamp.\n\n# References\n\n* [Timestamp Considerations in RFC 9562](https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#section-6.1)\n* [UUID Generator States in RFC 9562](https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#section-6.3)"
    }
